"""Generate release documentation from the actual seed and executed QA records."""
import json,sqlite3
from pathlib import Path
from database.store import connect,counts
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
db=connect(ROOT/'data/nilephytodock.sqlite');n=counts(db);db.close()
base=json.loads((ROOT/'data/literature/reviewed_manifest.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
six=json.loads((ROOT/'data/literature/six_oils_manifest.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
major=json.loads((ROOT/'data/literature/comprehensive_manifest.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
intro=f"NilePhytoDock Studio 0.6.0 is a native Windows molecular-screening application developed by **Ahmed G Soliman and Malak Taha**. The application and its external documentation are English."
inventory=f"The seed contains **{n['botanical_oils']} distinct botanical oils ({n['essential_oils']} essential and {n['fixed_oils']} fixed)**, **{n['unique_ready']} distinct ready InChIKeys**, {n['ready']} ready compound-name records, {n['compounds']} normalized name records, {n['species']} botanical taxa, {n['profiles']} analytical profiles and {n['records']} source observations. The {n['compounds']-n['ready']} remaining names need review. Repeated profiles, source peaks and aliases do not inflate the home-page counters."
limits="Docking scores and oil indices are computational screening priorities. They do not establish affinity, potency, efficacy, safety or mixture synergy. GC peak area is not an absolute mass fraction. Preparation uses a general protonation approximation, does not rebuild missing loops or side chains, and does not enumerate a pH-dependent ligand ensemble. One BEN/3PTB redocking system is not broad validation. Windows 11 on the current host is tested; Windows 10, a clean VM and all GPU configurations are untested. The executable is unsigned. PyMOL is optional and is not bundled."
oiltable='| Candidate | Decision and actual origin | Primary analytical source |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n'
for name,pmc,description in [('Sweet Marjoram','PMC9563047','Added; Origanum majorana, Giza Egypt; full supplementary DOCX GC table'),('Thyme','PMC9605189','Already present; Thymus vulgaris, Egyptian sample; not duplicated'),('Peppermint','PMC5527698','Added; Mentha × piperita, Taounate Morocco reference; not Egyptian'),('Sweet Basil','PMC9578474','Added; Ocimum basilicum, Tanta Egypt'),('Fennel','PMC11866597','Added; Foeniculum vulgare, experimental cultivation control; exact field coordinates unreported'),('Cumin','PMC9570728','Added; Cuminum cyminum, Egyptian market; growing origin unverified')]:
 oiltable+=f'| {name} | {description} | [{pmc}](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/{pmc}/) |\n'
workflow="""1. Extract the complete Windows ZIP. Keep `_internal` beside `NilePhytoDock.exe` and launch the 0.6 shortcut. Wait for Engines available.
2. Select the intended analytical profiles in Botanical library. Inspect geography, extraction, original units and source notes.
3. Import PDB/mmCIF receptors in Protein targets. Inspect chains, missing residues, ligands, waters, cofactors and metals.
4. In Screening setup set the study name, preparation choices and specific bound residues to remove. `BEN A:1` is only the supplied 3PTB example.
5. Run Prepare and predict all. Select a P2Rank pocket for each receptor. Automatic mode transfers its actual center and dimensions to the Smina protocol; Custom box records explicit coordinates.
6. Set exhaustiveness, scoring function, pose count, CPU count, seed and a writable output folder. Start the study and inspect progress and per-job status.
7. Open a saved pose from Docking results. Inspect the actual 3D geometry and Classic/Circular/Functional group 2D diagram. Select a contact row to focus the residue.
8. Read priorities together with coverage and source warnings. Concentration-based and headspace profiles receive no oil index.
9. Use Charts for supported plots, filters, hover values and point details. Export the actual plotted data alongside PNG/SVG/PDF figures and CSV/XLSX data.
10. Export reports and preserve the complete study directory, including Project_Data/project.nile.sqlite. Open Saved Project reopens its recorded calculations.
"""
visual="""The interaction palette is shared across 2D, 3D and charts: hydrogen bonds blue/dashed; hydrophobic green/dotted; ionic orange; pi-pi purple; pi-cation magenta; van der Waals gray; metal gold. Residue fills independently encode polarity, charge, biochemical class, amino-acid identity , hydrophobicity, aromaticity or interaction participation. The latter uses segmented 2D rings for multiple categories. Charge uses the prepared residue formal charge where available and an explicitly stated general convention otherwise.

Classic uses ordered rails; Circular arranges collision-checked residue circles around the ligand. A minimum-distance link per residue/type reduces clutter; parentheses count contacts. The complete atom pairs remain in SVG tooltips and source tables. 2D line lengths are schematic and labels report actual 3D distances.

The 3D viewer offers nine protein representations, three ligand styles, eight standard color modes, surfaces, site and contact filters, labels, interaction focus and reset/fit. Structural confidence requires explicit confirmation that B values contain pLDDT. Crystallographic B factors are never automatically treated as confidence. Contact-endpoint hydrogens remain chemically bonded and visible. Ring contacts use actual centroids. Protein/ligand atom coordinates are checked again after parsing in the browser.

Export 2D SVG and PNG at 300/600 DPI, 3D PNG at 2400×1800 or 4800×3600 pixels with matching DPI metadata, complex PDB, saved ligand SDF and PyMOL PML. PSE export is enabled only when an installed legitimate PyMOL is available.
"""
charts="""Sixteen chart types use saved calculations: docking heatmap; compound–protein bubbles; oil–protein bubbles; oil ranking; compound ranking; interaction matrix; interaction network; residue frequency; compound–oil relationship network; multitarget comparison. Unsupported plots are disabled.

Compound bubbles preserve source-profile-specific membership. Color and marker identify botanical oil; area is uniform or original GC peak area using one scale across all oils. Concentrations in other units cannot enter GC area sizing. Oil bubbles use normalized oil index or screened original GC area. Filters do not recalculate the study's original priority population. Heatmaps distinguish missing cells; interaction matrices preserve multiple categories per cell. Network source-membership edges are distinguished from classified molecular contacts. Exports include PNG, SVG, PDF, CSV and the plotted JSON specification.
"""
science="""P2Rank 2.5.1 with bundled Temurin Java 17.0.19 predicts pockets on the prepared receptor. The selected per-target center and dimensions are recorded and passed unchanged to native Smina 2020.12.10. Actual commands, seed, scoring function, input files and engine versions accompany results. RDKit 2026.09.1 validates molecular graphs and prepares ETKDGv3 conformers (seed 20261029), followed by converged MMFF94s or UFF optimization; Meeko generates PDBQT. ProLIF 2.2.3 classifies contacts on chemically typed RDKit graphs. PLIP is not used.

Contacts retain original atom indices, residue/chain/sequence/insertion identifiers, protein identity, method, parameters and geometry version `atom-anchors-3`. Hydrogen-bond distance joins donor and acceptor heavy atoms; the donor-H-acceptor angle is independently recomputed. Aromatic contacts use ring centroids and normal/plane geometry. Metal classification is restricted to complete chemically plausible Zn tetrahedral or Mg octahedral shells. Geometry mismatches fail visibly. Reanalysis first succeeds, then archives old records in `interaction_reanalyses` before replacing contacts. Raw docking scores and saved poses are preserved.

Exact normalized PubChem synonyms, accepted RDKit connectivity, single-component identity, molecular formula and source stereochemistry are checked independently. Unresolved stereocenters or required E/Z assignments are not approved. A source-geometry review withdrew 17 earlier automated approvals while retaining candidate files and audit data. Formula agreement with a PubChem CID verifies the resolved structure's consistency, not the identity of a tentative chromatographic peak.

Within each target, identical InChIKeys count once in the percentile population. With average ascending energy rank r among N identities, q=(N−r)/(N−1); a singleton receives 0.5. Oil index is sum(w*q)/sum(w) over successful, eligible constituents with original positive GC peak-area weights w. Coverage is the unnormalized sum of screened original areas; below 70% is flagged. Duplicate chemical identities in one profile block its index. Source-review observations cannot contribute to coverage, even if an older docking result exists. HPLC, qualitative LC-MS, headspace and fatty-acid pools have no oil index. Missing positive-weight targets make multitarget priority unavailable rather than being silently reweighted. Sensitivity varies one abundance at a time by ±10%.
"""
database="""Three reviewed literature packs retain 90 analytical profiles and 1448 observations from 37 primary PMC papers. The original 661 composition records survive unchanged. Original table rows, values, units, uncertainty, source names, PMCID/DOI, table/row IDs, sample origin and cached-file SHA-256 remain traceable. Import hashes make repeat imports idempotent; incompatible changed manifests require reviewed migration. A SQLite backup is created before merging a new bundled literature pack into an existing user library.

The supplied combined CSV is integrated with a source-audit table: 434 corroborating duplicates, 85 source differences retained for review and 64 additional source values. Raw Word rows remain intact. No missing values become zero; unknown peaks, class totals, retention indices and oil yield are not compounds. Partial major-component tables remain labeled partial; percentages are not normalized to 100%.

Peppermint's published methyl acetate at RI1295 is retained but source-specific docking eligibility is false pending review; it is not silently changed to menthyl acetate. Its rounded individual rows sum to 99.52% although the printed total says 99.51%. Cumin is a market sample, peppermint a Moroccan reference, and selected grape, hibiscus and olive growing origins are unverified. Jasmine headspace is not extracted essential oil; olive fatty-acid pools are not native free-fatty-acid or triglyceride molecular compositions. Nymphaea alba is supported; the contradictory blue-lily article and unavailable olive annotation table were excluded.
"""
build="""Use Windows x64 and the tested Python 3.12 environment. Install `requirements.txt`, retain third-party notices and restore the external runtime directories from the verified release (see `external_tools/ASSET_MANIFEST.json`). Native runtimes are release assets rather than large Git source blobs. Source includes exact hashes and upstream provenance; no engine rebuild is claimed.

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q
.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m PyInstaller --noconfirm --distpath dist_comprehensive --workpath build/pyinstaller_comprehensive build/NilePhytoDock.spec
```

For an actual installation check, set a fresh private `NILEPHYTODOCK_DATA` directory and run `NilePhytoDock.exe --verify-installation OUTPUT tests/fixtures/3PTB.pdb`. This performs real P2Rank and three Smina jobs, validates transferred boxes, checks HPLC index suppression and reports, and loads native 3D/Plotly canvases. Normal startup does not enter this path. The test needs a fresh output folder.

The supplied seed has zero research projects. A writable user copy under `%LOCALAPPDATA%/NilePhytoDock` stores projects. Preserve it and complete study folders before upgrades. Seven icon resolutions are embedded in the PE; shortcuts use the explicit ICO and the process sets AppUserModelID `NilePhytoDock.Studio`. The splash uses the supplied logo. English guides are copied to `Documentation` beside the executable, outside `_internal` and outside the application interface.
"""
analysis_methods="""

Functional groups are assigned with versioned atom-centred SMARTS and specific-class precedence. Explicit-H contacts map to their bonded heavy atom. Conventional groups and overlapping aromatic, alkene and hydrophobic features remain separate domains. Presence is distinct from directly participating atoms; event counts, unique InChIKeys and ligand-residue pairs are reported separately.

Chemical similarity uses Morgan radius 2, 2048 bits, chirality and Tanimoto; Butina clusters use a 0.65 similarity threshold. Site interaction similarity is binary chain/residue/insertion/category Jaccard within one prepared receptor and pocket. Two empty fingerprints are unavailable. Approximate classical MDS uses structural distances independently of scores.

Exploratory enrichment requires at least 12 structural-cluster representatives, selected lexicographically by InChIKey independently of score. Two-sided Fisher tests compare top/bottom energy quartiles with ties, with BH correction over tested groups. A small or redundant cohort is explicitly withheld. Associations do not establish activity or causation.

Export Interaction Table supports complete, best pose, selected protein, selected compound, group summary and frequency summary modes. CSV/XLSX retain full values and metadata; DOCX preserves required identities, source profiles, geometry, group atoms and methods, grouping repeated identifiers by pose. Empty scientific exports fail visibly.
"""
heritage="""

The preparation filter distinguishes Essential Oils, Fixed Oils, Botanical Extracts, Resins and Aromatic Preparations and Individual Natural Compounds. The Ancient Egyptian Botanical Heritage view evaluates 12 candidates with evidence type, period, confidence, source and taxonomic scope. Genus-level biomarkers do not establish a modern species; reconstructed recipes and uncertain ancient plant names are identified as interpretations. Modern analytical chemistry is stored separately from historical associations.

Fixed-oil fatty-acid pools do not establish native free-acid abundance. Unresolved Moringa sum lipids, analytical TMS derivatives, silicone contaminants and source-suspect assignments are blocked. Structures beyond 900 Da, 80 heavy atoms or 25 rotatable bonds require specialist review. Candidate files, original observations and existing raw results survive these eligibility changes.
"""
science+=analysis_methods+heritage
database+=heritage
visual+="\n\nThree actual appearance presets (Scientific Classic, High Contrast and Publication Quality) control background, protein/surface opacity, ligand carbon color, optional protein color, labels, outline material, ambient occlusion and fog. Split, 3D focus and 2D focus views make the canvas usable at smaller sizes. The former automatic 0.33 protein opacity has been removed.\n"
charts+=analysis_methods
for p in major['profiles']:
 oiltable+=f"| {p['common_name']} | {p['species']}; {p['category']}; {p['origin']} | [{p['pmcid']}](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/{p['pmcid']}/) |\n"

def write(path,text):
 p=ROOT/path;p.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True,parents=True);p.write_text(text.rstrip()+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
write('README.md','# NilePhytoDock Studio 0.6.0\n\n'+intro+'\n\n'+inventory+'\n\n## Start\n\n'+workflow+'\n## Documentation\n\n[User guide](docs/USER_GUIDE.md) · [Scientific methods](docs/SCIENTIFIC_METHODOLOGY.md) · [Database guide](docs/DATABASE_GUIDE.md) · [Developer guide](docs/DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md) · [Validation](docs/VALIDATION_REPORT.md) · [Software summary](SOFTWARE_SUMMARY.md) · [Continuation notes](NEXT_CODEX_PROMPT.md). PDF/DOCX manuals accompany the release.\n\n## Changes\n\n'+visual+'\n'+charts+'\n## Six-oil review\n\n'+oiltable+'\n## Limits\n\n'+limits+'\n\nSee [LICENSES.md](LICENSES.md) for bundled components and corresponding-source provenance.')
write('docs/USER_GUIDE.md','# User guide — 0.6.0\n\n'+intro+'\n\n'+workflow+'\n## Library\n\n'+inventory+'\n\n'+database+'\n## Visualization\n\n'+visual+'\n## Charts\n\n'+charts+'\n## Interpretation\n\n'+limits)
write('docs/SCIENTIFIC_METHODOLOGY.md','# Scientific methodology — 0.6.0\n\n'+intro+'\n\n'+science+'\n## Display semantics\n\n'+visual+'\n## Limits\n\n'+limits)
refs={**base['references'],**six['references'],**major['references']}
references='\n'.join(f"- [{pmc}: {r['title']}]({r['url']}) — DOI {r['doi']}" for pmc,r in refs.items())
write('docs/DATABASE_GUIDE.md','# Database guide — 0.6.0\n\n'+inventory+'\n\n'+database+'\n## Six-oil review\n\n'+oiltable+'\n## Primary sources\n\n'+references+'\n\nThe external Literature_Catalog_EN.csv and Literature_Observations_EN.csv describe the three reviewed literature packs. Full seed records remain available in SQLite.')
write('docs/DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md','# Developer guide — 0.6.0\n\n'+intro+'\n\n'+build+'\n## Architecture\n\n`UpgradeMixin → StudioMixin → RedesignMixin → BaseWindow` preserves the existing desktop workflow. `database` contains migrations and importers; `scientific` owns preparation, pockets, docking, geometry and ranking; `visualization` owns shared semantics, 2D/3D, charts and exports; `reporting` emits source observations and actual result tables. `app/chart_workspace.py` hosts offline Plotly 3.3.0 with a Qt WebChannel for selection details. No remote scripts are needed for normal screening.\n\n## Verification commands\n\n```powershell\npython -m tools.validate_redesign data/validation/NEW_workflow\npython -m tools.validate_upgrade_geometry\npython -m tools.validate_upgrade_charts\npython -m tools.verify_library_formulas\npython -m tools.verify_english_release\n```\n\nThe geometry/chart helpers use private copies of actual study results. Do not use them against live user data. Source imports, source-specific eligibility and identity approvals are separate gates. Do not promote a candidate solely to increase a displayed count.')
write('docs/INSTALLATION.md','# Installation — 0.6.0\n\nExtract the entire Windows release ZIP and double-click NilePhytoDock.exe. Keep `_internal` beside it. No administrator install, system Java or separately installed docking engine is required. Use the versioned 0.6 shortcut and its supplied icon. Documentation is English and external.\n\n'+build+'\n'+limits)
write('docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md','# Troubleshooting — 0.6.0\n\nIf the old icon/version appears, open the versioned 0.6 shortcut. Preserve the whole portable directory. Check Settings and process logs when an engine is unavailable. Select a predicted pocket for every target before automatic screening. Review structure status and source eligibility when a profile has no ready ligands. A blank oil index may be correct for HPLC, headspace, duplicate identities or incomplete results. Geometry mismatches must be repaired by inspecting source files and reanalysis, never by moving a plotted endpoint. Keep source, prepared structures, pose files and project snapshot together when reopening a study.\n\n'+limits)
write('CHANGELOG.md','# Changelog\n\n## 0.6.0 — 2026-10-29\n\n- Minimal dashboard counts distinct botanical oils and verified chemical structures from SQLite.\n- Versioned, independently verified atom/feature geometry and archived interaction reanalysis.\n- Classic/Circular/Functional group 2D diagrams, independent residue colors and shared interaction palette.\n- Offline 3D representation, surface, color, label, focus and high-resolution export controls.\n- Sixteen data-driven charts with bubble-area choices, filters, multiple membership and tabular exports.\n- Five missing oils added; existing thyme retained, with source-specific identity and geography review.\n- Stricter E/Z identity gate and InChIKey-based percentile/duplicate handling.\n- English-only interface and external English PDF/DOCX guides, source observations in reports.\n- Updated icon resources, Windows branding, source/build/release verification and GitHub distribution.\n\nOriginal working data and earlier release artifacts are preserved.')
write('SOFTWARE_SUMMARY.md','# NilePhytoDock — software summary\n\n'+intro+'\n\n'+inventory+'\n\nThe application connects documented plant chemistry, receptor preparation, P2Rank binding sites, native Smina calculations and geometry-verified molecular contacts in one local workflow. Each study retains source and prepared structures, exact pocket boxes and commands, pose and complex files, contact records, composition-aware priorities, figures and reproducible reports.\n\n'+visual+'\n'+charts+'\n'+oiltable+'\n## Scientific scope\n\n'+limits+'\n\nThe release evidence is indexed in docs/VALIDATION_REPORT.md. The portable distribution and complete English documentation are delivered under X:/nile/release. Repository: https://github.com/ahmedGSoliman99/NilePhytoDock. Versioned release: https://github.com/ahmedGSoliman99/NilePhytoDock/releases/tag/v0.6.0. Access requires the owner’s private-repository permissions.')
write('NEXT_CODEX_PROMPT.md','# Continuation instructions — NilePhytoDock 0.6.0\n\nContinue the existing native Windows project. Read README.md, docs/SCIENTIFIC_METHODOLOGY.md, docs/DATABASE_GUIDE.md and docs/VALIDATION_REPORT.md before edits. Developers are Ahmed G Soliman and Malak Taha. Keep all application text English and all user guides external and English. Preserve the supplied logo, seven-size ICO, splash, P2Rank-to-Smina box transfer, settings and saved projects.\n\n'+inventory+'\n\n'+science+'\n## Next useful work\n\nValidate on a clean Windows 10/11 VM and additional GPU/display configurations; broaden external redocking benchmarks; implement a deliberate curator workflow for the 633 unresolved names and source-identity observations; add independently reviewed Egyptian-source peppermint and other oil profiles when primary analytical evidence supports them. Do not describe these future tasks as implemented. No code-signing certificate or proprietary PyMOL is supplied.\n\nUse a fresh private data/output directory for tests. Back up SQLite with its backup API, not a raw WAL-era file copy. Never replace user projects with a seed. Raw docking energies/poses remain immutable; changed derived indices must retain the curation context. Git history begins from the owner-authorized current source snapshot because no repository history existed in this workspace. Never rewrite or invent earlier authorship. Native binary distribution belongs in GitHub Releases. Preserve actual authenticated account identity for commits.\n\n'+build)
print(n)
